  "title": "Hilde B Probable NDE 4419",
  "date": "'July, 2008'",
  "content": "Medical Center 2008 I could not bear the burning pain and wanted to die. Delmar, my husband, held me in his arms. I begged him to let me die. I knew that he could not bear seeing me in that much pain. He held me closer and closer. No more pain. Death is merciful. Zoë was leaving her body, soaring through pitch black space of profound peace. Reaching her own origins, at the beginning of time, No words can describe those Feelings of belonging, She was part of all there is She was home. There was no tunnel of light, no angels to greet her. Protected and content She was granted a glance into life after death For a split second? For minutes? She doesn't know. She was whole. She had to return to her body To finish a task. of forgiveness, to heal and to love , Knowing that soon she has to leave the body again, for a new beginning. Comfort Like an atom, neutron, or proton, soul is the smallest particle there is and the most powerful of all. Soul is eternal. Zoe is life, and a name for soul.",
